<title>USA: Transaction Network sets share buyback.</title>
<headline>Transaction Network sets share buyback.</headline>
<dateline>RESTON, Va. 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transaction Network Services Inc said its board has authorized the repurchase of an unspecified number of its common shares.</p>
<p>Company spokeswoman Karen Kazmark declined to specify the number of shares to be bought back, saying the company simply chose not to disclose the data at this time.  She did not elaborate.</p>
<p>The company said the full or partial execution of the repurchase program is dependent on the price of the company's stock and prevailing market conditions.</p>
<p>Transaction Network, a communications services company, was up 7/8 to 10-7/8 in mid-afternoon trading on the Nasdaq.</p>
